Z||000000||862M4inCA||10-15-2000||06:22 AM||||Have noticed the last couple days that my engine while driving seems to have very little power, especially when I'm accelerating at a mild/moderate rate, almost to the point I'm NOT accelerating, but maintaining my speed. However when I push the accelerator 3/4 of the way or more I get a LARGE boost of power. Wonder if this is a tell tale sign of my TPS going south...Kinda hope not since that's an expensive little sucker and I replaced it less than a year ago. I haven't noticed any any codes being stored into the computer, and have checked all my vacuum connections as well as timing. So far everything appears to be correct. Also, just recently it had the fuel injector and pump replaced, and dont think these are faulty. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-15-2000||11:39 AM||||check the MAP sensor carfully, especially the line to it. make sure it's not pinched/blocked in addition to not leaking. make sure it's connected to the right location on the engine and that port isn't blocked either.<P>try another MAP sensor. These don't go bad often and don't have moving parts. A used one will likely work for testing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||862M4inCA||10-17-2000||03:09 AM||||Well, I checked all the vacuum connections by spraying carb cleaner all over them, and the engine just sat and idled. So I'm thinking that there isn't a cracked hose. I also took the hose to the MAP loose and blew through it, and established that it's NOT pluged, however I noticed that the rubber end on the side that goes into the TBI unit was torn on the edge, but after doucing it with carb spray, I still couldn't get the engine to fluctuate any. Only other option, IF it's the MAP, is to try another. Wish I had another GM product around to swipe the MAP off of for a minute.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Guess it's down to the boneyard to grab one or two to use them for testing. Thanx for leading me in that direction tho.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||10-17-2000||01:23 PM||||just unplug your MAP to put the ECM into "Limp Home" mode. ||||reg||1
